  "answer": "The actuarial-services RFPs propose these terms. Where an RFP gives no specific renewal period, I have not inferred one.\n\n| RFP | Initial term and renewal or extension option |\n|---|---|\n| [Stoneham, pp. 3, 5](Stoneham_MA__Request-for-proposals---Actuarial-Services-PDF.pdf#page=3) | Agreement **not to exceed seven years**, covering the 2020, 2022, and 2024 valuations. It does not separate an initial term from an extension option. |\n| [Boston, p. 5](Boston__RFP_Actuarial_and_Consulting_Services_for_Pension_Benefits_08-30-2022.pdf#page=5) | **Five years**, with the Board able to extend it for **one or two additional years** without readvertising. |\n| [Illinois SRS, pp. 3, 34](Illinois_SRS__RFP--Actuarial_Consulting_Services--SRS.pdf#page=3) | **Five years**, July 1, 2024–June 30, 2029; no specific renewal option stated. |\n| [COAERS, pp. 4, 18](COAERS__COAERS_Actuarial_Services_RFP_June_26_2025.pdf#page=4) | **Five-year master agreement**, January 1, 2026–December 31, 2030, with annual engagement letters; no specific extension option stated. |\n| [LACERS, p. 3](LACERS__2025_actuarial_consulting_services_rfp.pdf#page=3) | **Three years**, potentially followed by **up to two one-year extensions**. |\n| [Apple Valley Fire Protection District, pp. 3–4](AVFPD__RFP-Actuatial-Services-2024.pdf#page=3) | Work is specified through **June 2029**—2024, 2026, and 2028 valuations plus intervening roll-forwards. The RFP mentions **optional contract extensions**, with fees negotiated when exercised, but does not specify their length or a separately stated initial contract term. |\n| [St. Louis Police Retirement System, p. 7](St_Louis_PRS__PRS_Actuarial_Auditor_Services_RFP_and_Questionnaire.pdf#page=7) | An initial **one-time engagement**, with PRS retaining an **option to renew**; no renewal length is specified. |\n| [KCERA, p. 17](KCERA__RFP_2024_Actuarial_Audit_Final_-_with_Sample_Agreement.pdf#page=17) | **One year** from final contract execution; no renewal option stated. |",
